WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.977
Not every value made of digits should be numeric.

00:00:02.977 --> 00:00:06.657
Some values are identifiers rather than quantities.

00:00:06.657 --> 00:00:10.907
Take employee ID zero zero one two five.

00:00:10.907 --> 00:00:14.342
We do not add or average employee IDs.

00:00:14.342 --> 00:00:16.972
We use them to identify records.

00:00:16.972 --> 00:00:21.315
If we store that ID as a number, the leading zeros disappear.

00:00:21.776 --> 00:00:28.718
The same issue appears with ZIP codes, account numbers, product codes, and many other identifiers.

00:00:28.718 --> 00:00:36.433
A better question than “Does this value contain digits?” is “Do I plan to calculate with this value?” If not,

00:00:36.433 --> 00:00:42.059
and the exact formatting matters, text is often the right choice.
